From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:50:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix undo doing nothing once the history is full

react-use's useStateWithHistory leaves its position one past the last
entry once capacity (100) is reached, so the first undo after every edit
restored the current state and appeared to do nothing. Replace it with
our own pure history implementation (with tests).

Also make a timeline drag of a segment a single undo step, instead of
one step per mouse move, which filled the history very quickly.

